+Each call to an outside service (OpenCode, Speechify, R2) goes through `outbound.request` (`src/outbound.zig`): 4 tries in all (1 + 3 retries), waiting 5 s, 30 s, then 2 min between them. A network error, a timeout, a 429 or a 5xx is a failed try and is retried; a `Retry-After` in seconds on a 429 or a 503 replaces the scheduled wait, capped at 2 min. Any other status, a 4xx included, ends the call at once with that status.
+
+Zig's HTTP client can time out neither a connect nor an idle read, so the limit is applied around each try: a try that hasn't got its whole answer 60 s after it started fails as a timeout. So a connect that hangs fails at 60 s rather than the owner's 10 s, an answer that stalls fails 60 s after the try started rather than after 60 s with no byte, and an answer still arriving after 60 s fails too.
 
